  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the exponential function $y=k\\times a^x$, where $a>0$, that passes through the following points.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(1,4)$ and $(4,32)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=2\\times 2^x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4&=ka\\\\32&=ka^4\\end{align*}$$\n\nDivide the second equation by the first.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a^3&=\\frac{32}{4}\\\\a^3&=8\\\\a&=2\\\\k&=\\frac{4}{2}\\\\k&=2\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $y=2\\times 2^x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(1,2)$ and $(4,16)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=2^x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2&=ka\\\\16&=ka^4\\end{align*}$$\n\nDivide the second equation by the first.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a^3&=\\frac{16}{2}\\\\a^3&=8\\\\a&=2\\\\k&=\\frac{2}{2}\\\\k&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $y=2^x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(0,2)$ and $(2,18)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=2\\times 3^x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2&=ka^0\\\\k&=2\\\\18&=2a^2\\\\a^2&=9\\\\a&=3\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $a>0$, take the positive square root. Therefore $y=2\\times3^x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(1,20)$ and $(-1,0.8)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=4\\times 5^x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}20&=ka\\\\0.8&=ka^{-1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nDivide the first equation by the second.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2&=\\frac{20}{0.8}\\\\a^2&=25\\\\a&=5\\\\k&=\\frac{20}{5}\\\\k&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $a>0$, use the positive root. Therefore $y=4\\times5^x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
  },
